Encoding: UTF-8
Type: Package
Package: susieRsmall
Title: Sum of Single Effects Regression with a Small-Sample NIG Prior
Description: Implements variable selection in linear regression using the
    "Sum of Single Effects" (SuSiE) model, as described in Wang et al
    (2020) <DOI:10.1101/501114> and Zou et al
    (2021) <DOI:10.1101/2021.11.03.467167>. Provides Gaussian and corrected
    normal-inverse-gamma single-effect updates, with the latter integrating
    residual-variance uncertainty for small-sample analyses. Returns posterior
    inclusion probabilities and credible sets for genetic fine-mapping and
    other sparse regression applications. Distributed as the distinct package
    'susieRsmall' so it can be installed alongside 'susieR' and compared using
    'susieRsmall::susie()' and 'susieR::susie()' in the same R session.
    The normal-inverse-gamma method is selected explicitly with prior = 'nig'.
